WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.168
-Now, after six seasons,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.536
you guys have gotten
pretty close.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.970
I wanted to see
just how close you are

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.107
in a game we call
Know Your "Schitts Creek."

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.608
Here's how the game works.

00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:11.544
One of you will wear
noise-canceling headphones

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.846
while the other three answer
a question about you.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:14.981
Then you'll take
the headphones off,

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.882
and we'll see
if your answer matches.

00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:18.183
Make sense?
-I'm scared.

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:19.385
-Let's do this.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:20.753
Eugene, the first question
is about you,

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:21.954
so please put these on.

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.823
-You have to put it
over your hair, Dad.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.224
-Oh, boy. Oh, boy.

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:26.860
-Okay.
-No, you don't.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.694
-I wonder if it's gonna
touch your hair.

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:32.665
-What's the biggest pet peeve
Eugene had to overcome on set?

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.700
-Oh.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.767
-Something to do with food?

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.235
-No, his hair.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.037
-Oh, maybe it's the hair.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.204
It's the hair.

00:00:39.204 --> 00:00:40.440
Getting his hair wet.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.142
-It's "The Drip."
Getting his hair wet. 100%.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.043
-Yeah, that or working
with his kids.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.512
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.748
-Eugene, here we go.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:52.785
The question was,
what was the biggest pet peeve

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:55.488
Eugene had to overcome on set?

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.457
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:00.059
-No, you can't put it back on!

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:00.960
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.362
-Oh, "The Drip."

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:06.766
The episode in the show
when my hair's soaking wet

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.101
and I have to...

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.702
-Wow, that's what they all said.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.903
[ Ding ]

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.372
They all said that.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.607
That was it.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.776
-Catherine said your kids
were a close second.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.910
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.714
-A close second.
Nothing comes close to the hair.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.184
Anyway.
-Alright, here we go.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.352
That's it. That's the music.
It's working.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.720
Alright, Catherine.
This is for Catherine.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.456
Alright.
-Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:34.493
-What's the hardest Catherine
laughed while shooting?

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:35.928
-[ Exhales sharply ]

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:43.002
I would say it was a scene
called "Allez Vous,"

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.004
and it was a scene that she --

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:49.508
-She and I were selling
[Clears throat]

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:52.077
cosmetics to the town,

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:55.715
and it was just a sad, desperate
sales pitch that was not --

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.617
-But you had some
of the product...

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.319
-Dan's face was orange.
-...on his face,

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.253
so he looked bronzy,
bronzy, bronzy.

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:02.856
-It was bad. It was --

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.124
-Catherine started the scene

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.926
and could not look at him
without laughing.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.628
That's my guess.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.829
-You guys agree?

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.096
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-That's the one? Alright.

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.098
Alright.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.566
Catherine. Okay.
Alright, ready?

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.902
-I was afraid to look
at you 'cause I thought,

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.704
"What if I find out
I'm a lip reader?"

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.505
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.274
I actually kept my face away.
-You just found out now.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.942
-Wouldn't that have been
a wonderful discovery?

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.276
-Yeah, but not here.
-The question was,

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:26.746
what's the hardest Catherine
laughed while shooting.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.381
-I bet that's easy.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.349
Um...

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.385
I think it was when

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:35.622
Daniel and I were doing
"Allez Vous," and --

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.989
[ Cheering ]

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:38.324
[ Ding ]

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.492
-Whoo!

00:02:40.492 --> 00:02:42.862
-Because he was so --

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.831
David, the character
was so nervous

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.032
trying to sell this product,

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.268
and he had also tested
out the tanning cream,

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.369
and it was a yellow, orange,

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.672
and he looked like
a goldfish caught in headlights.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.273
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.008
-Not wrong.
-I couldn't stop.

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:57.343
I was so unprofessional.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.545
-Those are, like,
the best moments, though.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.013
I love it.
-We are two for two.

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.982
Not that I've been counting
or that I'm competitive, but...

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.651
-Yeah, you guys know each other.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.818
-They do that. They do that.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.053
-This could have gone
really bad.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.222
Imagine we know nothing
about each other.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.723
Just failed every question.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.391
-Well, here we go.
We have one more.

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:14.994
Alright, on the show, the
Rose family fell from riches.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:18.831
In real life, how did Dan make
his first dollar?

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:22.101
-Oh, didn't he work at Baby Gap
or something?

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.068
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:24.536
-Gap Kids.

00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:25.738
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.905
-Aww.

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:28.340
-Well, babysitting before that?

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.442
-No.
-No entertaining your guests?

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:31.711
-Uh, no.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.412
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.114
-Did any of your guests
know you had a son?

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.350
-No babysitting 'cause
he doesn't like kids.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.851
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.453
-And kids don't like him.
-Another fact.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.787
-Yeah, Gap Kids.

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.822
-He's really getting into it.
He's very serious, yeah.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:45.224
-You guys ready?
Alright, Dan, here we go.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:46.425
-Yeah.

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:48.161
-On the show, the Rose family
fell from riches.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:53.466
In real life, how did you make
your first dollar?

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:57.569
-My parents dropped me off
in front of a Gap Kids

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:00.173
and said very clearly,

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:03.309
"Do not come home
without a job application."

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.311
And I don't want to say
that that's, like,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.080
motivated me to be
a compulsive over-worker,

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.583
but it definitely hasn't
not done that.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.017
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:13.152
[ Ding ]

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.554
-Gap Kids!
That's correct! Yes!

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.788
-Whoa!

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.723
Best that we've ever done!
-Oh, my goodness.

00:04:17.723 --> 00:04:19.124
-This is amazing. I love this.

00:04:19.124 --> 00:04:21.093
-Alright, three for three.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.028
-Annie, it's up to you.

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.497
I mean, the pressure's on.
Come on back.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.732
-It's a great song on there.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.533
-Thank you.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.634
-Okay.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:29.701
-Got it.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.203
-Okay, ready, guys?
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:34.641
-What's the biggest fight Annie
got in on set?

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:35.741
-A fight?

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:36.976
-Fight?

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.378
-What's, like,
the coffee too cold?

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.180
-Fist fight with me?

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.182
-I would say she's never
gotten into a fight

00:04:44.182 --> 00:04:45.551
about anything on set.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.052
-We got to think of something.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:48.654
She must have.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.957
-I just don't want to
lose the game. Um...

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.658
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.794
I don't remember a fight.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.061
-Yeah, that's what I'm saying.

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:57.830
-I would say this is
a trick question.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.565
She has not gotten into a fight.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.334
-She's a lovely Canadian girl.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.368
-Yeah.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.402
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.804
-This is so Canada right now.

00:05:05.804 --> 00:05:07.940
This is unbelievable.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.276
-I don't know.
We're not into conflict.

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:11.444
-Got you.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.345
-She's, like, too nice
to get into a fight, eh.

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:15.881
-I know. I'm sorry.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.817
-What if she says,
"Oh, which one would it be?"

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.185
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.753
-Alright, here we go.
Let's see if the answer...

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:21.788
Okay, good.

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:23.122
-Okay.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.491
-Making it super anxious
over there.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.159
-Oh, yeah. Tell the truth
on this one.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:28.261
Boy, oh, boy.

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.629
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:31.096
-I'm scared a bit.

00:05:31.096 --> 00:05:32.799
-Oh, so am I.

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:33.932
-Alright, the question was,

00:05:33.932 --> 00:05:36.802
what's the biggest fight
Annie got in on set?

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:39.105
-Biggest fight I got in on set?

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:41.374
-Yeah.
-Oh, um...

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:43.910
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.278
It was with Dan.

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:46.445
